      "writtenOn": "2025-05-01T13:49:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the old code\u0027s handling of explicit required alignment had a subtle bug where it adjusted `fOffset` but then if we overflowed the buffer, we used the now-modified `fOffset` as the total used.\n\n`fUsedSized` is only used for adjusting the size of the next block, so it wouldn\u0027t trigger catastrophic behavior, but I think it means we don\u0027t need to update `info-\u003efOffset \u003d offset` until we know we are in the non-overflowed buffer case. This should also let us return just std::optional\u003cuint32_t\u003e, like:\n```\nauto offset \u003d this-\u003ewillBufferOffsetOverflow(...);\nif (offset.has_value()) {\n   info.fOffset \u003d *offset;\n} else {\n   // overflowedBuffer code\n   offset \u003d 0;\n   // or we could set info.fOffset \u003d 0, but it\u0027s already being set to 0 when\n   // we get inside the if (!info.fBuffer) code and that is perhaps clearer?\n} \n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 569,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 569,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "78a5c0278cf25fb08b83299e957a39c87f670a3e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
